- Story & Context: Legend spread across the Dutch delta of an abandoned grain carrier drifting through the mouth of the Scheldt, its ballast tanks flooded and its holds infested with millions of dormant overwintering moths. Harbor scavengers boarded the listing vessel under the sweep of pale searchlights, finding that the automated navigation beacon had fused with an ungrounded music box left running on the bridge, vibrating the iron deck plates at frequencies so warm and deep they coaxed the entire swarm from their cocoons into the freezing sea air. An unknown radio pirate captured the cloud of insects fluttering against the radar mast while the ship's horn bellowed out across the sandbars, singing through the tape crackle: "Breathe through the salt, little stranger, the channel is wide."
